{
  "format": 1,
  "side": "client",
  "comment": "kiln.vfx's VFX resource table at 4,096 (package 17a; docs/re/vfx.md 4.3.2, docs/kiln/services/vfx.md). VfxSystemCreate (caps/VfxCreateSystem) sizes the resource registry with five immediates: the GUID map's reserve request, which is also its count limit (caps/VfxMapReserveSite: lea rcx,[sys+caps/vfx.map]; mov r8d,caps/vfx.map_limit_request; call caps/VfxMapAllocate, which stores the request at map+caps/vfx.map_limit_relative), the record table's bytes, its initialisation count and its capacity field (caps/VfxTableAllocationSite: mov edx,caps/vfx.table_bytes; call alloc; mov [sys+caps/vfx.table],rax; mov ecx,caps/vfx.table_init_count; mov qword [sys+caps/vfx.table_capacity_offset],caps/vfx.table_capacity), and the pending-activation bit count (caps/VfxPendingResizeSite: mov r8d,caps/vfx.pending_bits; lea rcx,[sys+caps/vfx.pending]; call caps/VfxPendingResize; bit count at sys+caps/vfx.pending_count). caps/VfxTableInitLoop checks the record stride (caps/vfx.table_stride) of the initialisation loop; caps/VfxTableAliasCopy checks that the constructor copies the new table and its capacity to the alias at sys+caps/vfx.alias / +caps/vfx.alias_capacity; @caps/VfxInitResources.state reads the initialisation state byte (0 enlist, 1 waiting, 2 ready). The feature caps.vfx.expansion_sites says the sites resolve; it is not permission to patch: kiln.vfx compares every window byte for byte in memory before it writes (native/services/vfx/expand.cpp).",
